%I A398326 #10 Sep 07 2026 03:05:01
%S A398326 1,2,5,17,80,475,3848,39687,496430,7174735,116214038,2070929973,
%T A398326 40136039186,839342980334
%N A398326 Number of connected cubic simple graphs on 2n unlabeled nodes with chromatic index 3.
%C A398326 By Vizing's theorem the chromatic index of a cubic graph is either 3 or 4 (class 1 or class 2).
%H A398326 Jan Goedgebeur and Patric R. J. Östergård, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.01363">Switching 3-Edge-Colorings of Cubic Graphs</a>, arXiv:2105.01363 [math.CO], May 2021. See Table 1.
%H A398326 Brendan D. McKay and Gordon F. Royle, <a href="https://users.cecs.anu.edu.au/~bdm/papers/Gobstoppers.pdf">Constructing the cubic graphs on up to 20 vertices</a>, Ars Combinatoria, 21A (1986) 129-140. See pp. 137-138.
%H A398326 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Class1Graph.html">Class 1 Graph</a>.
%H A398326 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/CubicGraph.html">Cubic Graph</a>.
%F A398326 a(n) = A002851(n) - A357446(n).
%e A398326 a(5) = 17: of the 19 connected cubic graphs on 10 nodes, only two have chromatic index 4, the Petersen graph and the unique connected cubic graph on 10 nodes with a bridge.
%o A398326 (nauty) for n in {4..20..2}; do geng -qc -d3 -D3 $n | countg -q1 -A1; done
%Y A398326 Cf. A002851, A357446.
%K A398326 nonn,more,new
%O A398326 2,2
%A A398326 _Freddy Barrera_, Aug 31 2026
